From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Chapin <japhet@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:02:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] [PWA] Harden browser reuse in navigation capturing
 redirects

- Store `navigation_params_browser_` as a
  `base::WeakPtr<BrowserWindowInterface>` in
  `NavigationCapturingProcess` and verify liveness via
  `!IsBrowserClosing()` before reusing it for `kNavigateExisting` /
  `kFocusExisting` tab lookups or redirect reparenting.
- Verify `!IsBrowserClosing(browser)` and
  `browser->GetType() == (for_app_browser ? TYPE_APP : TYPE_NORMAL)` in
  `AppBrowserController::FindTopLevelBrowsingContextForWebApp()` and
  `FindForWebApp()`, and require `browser->GetType() == TYPE_APP` for
  `has_tab_strip` in `CreateWebAppBrowserController()`.
- Add `IsBrowserClosing()` and `CanReparentWebContentsIntoBrowser()` in
  `web_app_launch_utils` to verify that a target browser is live
  (`!IsDeleteScheduled()` and `!is_attempting_to_close_browser()`) and
  either a `TYPE_NORMAL` browser or a `TYPE_APP` web app window capable
  of accepting the tab (empty, tabbed via `has_tab_strip()`, or
  replacing a pinned home tab).
- Reuse `CanReparentWebContentsIntoBrowser()` across
  `ReparentToAppBrowser`, `ReparentWebContentsToTabbedBrowser` (via
  `FindNormalBrowser`), `GetInitialNavigationParamsOverride`, the
  `kNavigateNew` branches of `GetEffectiveClientModeAndBrowser`, and
  `ReparentWebContentsIntoAppBrowser`.
- Add `CHECK(CanReparentWebContentsIntoBrowser(...))` invariants in
  `NavigationCapturingProcess`, `ReparentWebContentsIntoAppBrowser`, and
  `ReparentWebContentsIntoBrowserImpl`.

Fixed: 573285920, 574907939
Test: NavigationCapturingControllableRedirectionBrowserNavigatorTest.*
Test: NavigationCapturingWithRedirectionBrowserNavigatorTest.*
Test: NavigationCapturingBrowserNavigatorBrowserTest.MiddleClickBrowserAppFromDocumentPictureInPicture
